---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import DataTable from '../components/DataTable.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import StateBlock from '../components/StateBlock.astro';
import StatusChip from '../components/StatusChip.astro';
import { loadCorpus } from '../lib/corpus';
import { longDate } from '../lib/cite';
import { CHANGE_LABEL, byYear, changeSummary, overdueFigures, recordedChanges, scheduledChanges } from '../lib/changes';
import { TODAY } from '../lib/today';
import { breadcrumbs, collectionPage, graph, organization, website } from '../lib/schema';

const corpus = await loadCorpus();
const recorded = recordedChanges(corpus);
const years = byYear(recorded);
const scheduled = scheduledChanges(corpus, TODAY);
const overdue = overdueFigures(corpus, TODAY);
const summary = changeSummary(corpus, TODAY);

const trail = [
	{ name: 'Home', path: '/' },
	{ name: 'What changed', path: '/changed' },
];

const jsonLd = graph(
	organization(),
	website(),
	breadcrumbs(trail),
	collectionPage({
		name: 'What changed',
		path: '/changed',
		description:
			'Every recorded change to the evidence base, dated, with the record that carries it, and every amount an instrument has scheduled to move.',
		items: recorded.slice(0, 40).map((c) => ({ name: c.title, path: c.path })),
	}),
);
---

<BaseLayout
	title="What changed"
	description="Every documented change to the sources behind this library: guidance rescinded, bills that never passed, forms superseded, documents re-read, corrections published, and the amounts their instruments have scheduled to move."
	jsonLd={jsonLd}
	pageType="editorial"
	machinePath="/changed.json"
>
	<PageHeader
		eyebrow="What changed"
		title="The evidence base moves, and this is the record of it moving"
		lede="Built from the source registry rather than written. A bill that failed, a guidance rescinded, a form edition superseded, a document returned to and re-read: each is already a field on a record, and this is those fields as one dated feed."
		trail={trail}
	/>

	<section class="band band-tight">
		<div class="shell answer-grid">
			<div class="prose">
				<Callout tone="limit">
					<p>
						<strong>This is what we have recorded, not what has happened.</strong> A change absent
						from this page is one this library has not recorded, which is a different statement
						from it not having occurred. The corpus is concentrated in California and holds{' '}
						{corpus.sources.length} documents in total, so read this as the movement of one
						evidence base rather than as the movement of insurance law.
					</p>
				</Callout>

				<h2 id="dates">Two kinds of date, and they are not the same</h2>
				<p>
					<strong>A recorded change is dated by when we recorded it.</strong> We know a guidance was
					rescinded because we read the notice saying so; the field does not tell us the date the
					decision was taken. Publishing our filing date as the event date would be a small
					inaccuracy repeated across every row, so it is labelled instead. Where the document states
					its own date, that date is in the note, in the document's words.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>A scheduled change is dated by the instrument.</strong> Those are the dates a
					statute or rule sets for itself, and they are the only forward-looking dates here.
				</p>

				<h2 id="scheduled">Scheduled to change</h2>
				<p>
					{scheduled.length} published {scheduled.length === 1 ? 'amount is' : 'amounts are'} moved
					by their own instrument on a date it names. This is the part nobody else publishes: a
					reserve, a limit selection or an internal guideline written against one of these is
					written against a number with an expiry date on it.
				</p>
				{
					scheduled.length > 0 ? (
						<DataTable
							caption="Amounts an instrument has scheduled to move, soonest first"
							columns={['Moves on', 'Amount today', 'What it is', 'What moves it']}
							rows={scheduled.map((s) => [
								longDate(s.date),
								s.amount,
								`${s.label}${s.states.length ? ` (${s.states.join(', ')})` : ''}`,
								s.movesWhen,
							])}
						/>
					) : (
						<StateBlock kind="empty" heading="No published amount has a scheduled move ahead of it.">
							<p>
								Every figure in the library either moves by amendment, which cannot be dated in
								advance, or has no scheduled move recorded.
							</p>
						</StateBlock>
					)
				}
				<p>
					<strong>We do not compute what the new amount will be.</strong> Several of these are
					stepped schedules whose operative value is arithmetic from the instrument rather than a
					figure it prints, and this library does not publish a number its source did not state.
					Each figure record carries that hedge in its own note; follow the row to{' '}
					<a href="/figures">the figure</a> for it.
				</p>

				<h2 id="recorded">Recorded changes</h2>
				<p>
					{summary.recorded} in total: {summary.notActive} documents that are no longer good
					authority, {summary.rechecks} documents returned to and re-read, and{' '}
					{summary.corrections} published {summary.corrections === 1 ? 'correction' : 'corrections'}{' '}
					to what this library said.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>A re-read is a comparison, not an outcome.</strong> It means somebody opened the
					document again and checked the operative language against what we had recorded from it.
					Where one found a discrepancy, the correction it produced is its own entry below — joined
					by having been made, not inferred from two nearby dates.
				</p>
				{
					recorded.length === 0 ? (
						<StateBlock kind="empty" heading="Nothing has been recorded as changed yet.">
							<p>
								The registry carries the fields this feed is built from. It is empty because
								nothing has moved since the library was written, not because nothing is watched.
							</p>
						</StateBlock>
					) : (
						years.map((group) => (
							<>
								<h3 id={`y${group.year}`}>{group.year}</h3>
								<div class="rows">
									{group.changes.map((change) => (
										<div class="row" style="grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr)">
											<div>
												<h4 class="row-title">
													<a href={change.path} style="text-decoration: none">{change.title}</a>
												</h4>
												<div class="row-meta">
													{change.kind === 'corrected' ? (
														<StatusChip kind="corrected" />
													) : (
														<span class="status status-plain">{CHANGE_LABEL[change.kind]}</span>
													)}
													<span class="meta">Recorded {longDate(change.date)}</span>
												</div>
												{change.detail && (
													<p style="margin-top: var(--s-2); font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--muted)">
														{change.detail}
													</p>
												)}
												{change.was && change.now && (
													<dl style="margin-top: var(--s-3); display: grid; gap: var(--s-2)">
														<dt class="meta">Previously said</dt>
														<dd style="margin: 0; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--muted)">
															{change.was}
														</dd>
														<dt class="meta">Now says</dt>
														<dd style="margin: 0; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--ink)">
															{change.now}
														</dd>
													</dl>
												)}
												{change.supersededBy && (
													<p style="margin-top: var(--s-2); font-size: var(--text-sm)">
														Replaced by{' '}
														<a href={change.supersededBy.path}>{change.supersededBy.title}</a>.
													</p>
												)}
											</div>
										</div>
									))}
								</div>
							</>
						))
					)
				}

				{
					overdue.length > 0 && (
						<>
							<h2 id="overdue">Scheduled moves already behind us</h2>
							<Callout tone="warn">
								<p>
									{overdue.length}{' '}
									{overdue.length === 1 ? 'figure names a move date' : 'figures name move dates'}{' '}
									that {overdue.length === 1 ? 'has' : 'have'} passed, so the published amount may
									no longer be the operative one. This is the registry reporting on itself rather
									than a change we are asserting, and it is a review trigger:{' '}
									{overdue.map((f) => `${f.label} (${f.nextMove})`).join('; ')}.
								</p>
							</Callout>
						</>
					)
				}

				<h2 id="how">How this is produced</h2>
				<p>
					Nobody writes it. Every source record carries <code>status</code>,{' '}
					<code>statusNote</code>, <code>lastChecked</code>, <code>lastCheckedBasis</code> and{' '}
					<code>supersededBy</code>; every published record can carry a correction; every figure
					records what moves it and when. This page is those fields assembled and sorted. That is
					why it cannot drift from the library: there is no prose here to fall out of date
					separately.
				</p>
				<p>
					It follows that the feed grows when the library is maintained, not when someone decides to
					publish news. A quarter with no entries is a quarter in which nothing was recorded as
					having moved, and that is worth knowing too.
				</p>
				<p>
					The same feed is machine-readable at <a href="/changed.json">/changed.json</a>, and the
					underlying records are in the{' '}
					<a href="/dataset">frozen dataset releases</a> with a checksum on every claim.
				</p>
			</div>

			<aside class="answer-rail" aria-label="Page contents">
				<nav class="rail-block" aria-labelledby="on-this-page">
					<h2 id="on-this-page">On this page</h2>
					<ol>
						<li><a href="#dates">Two kinds of date</a></li>
						<li><a href="#scheduled">Scheduled to change</a></li>
						<li><a href="#recorded">Recorded changes</a></li>
						{overdue.length > 0 && <li><a href="#overdue">Moves already behind us</a></li>}
						<li><a href="#how">How this is produced</a></li>
					</ol>
				</nav>
				<div class="rail-block">
					<h2>The feed</h2>
					<dl>
						<div><dt>Recorded changes</dt><dd>{summary.recorded}</dd></div>
						<div><dt>No longer authority</dt><dd>{summary.notActive}</dd></div>
						<div><dt>Documents re-read</dt><dd>{summary.rechecks}</dd></div>
						<div><dt>Corrections</dt><dd>{summary.corrections}</dd></div>
						<div><dt>Scheduled ahead</dt><dd>{summary.scheduled}</dd></div>
						<div><dt>Newest entry</dt><dd>{longDate(summary.newest)}</dd></div>
					</dl>
				</div>
				<div class="rail-block no-print">
					<h2>Related</h2>
					<ul>
						<li><a href="/sources">Source registry</a></li>
						<li><a href="/figures">Figures</a></li>
						<li><a href="/corrections">Corrections log</a></li>
						<li><a href="/dataset">Dataset releases</a></li>
						<li><a href="/methodology">Methodology</a></li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</aside>
		</div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
